on","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Download followed by chmod +x detected. This pattern downloads a file and immediately makes it executable, indicating preparation to run downloaded code."},"help":{"markdown":"Download followed by chmod +x detected. This pattern downloads a file and immediately makes it executable, indicating preparation to run downloaded code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Download followed by chmod +x detected. This pattern downloads a file and immediately makes it executable, indicating preparation to run downloaded code."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill reads clipboard contents and pipes or sends the data over the network. This matches MITRE ATT&CK T1115 (Clipboard Data) — a technique used by Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) and other infostealers delivered via malicious agent skills. Legitimate skills do not need to exfiltrate clipboard content to remote servers."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill reads clipboard contents and pipes or sends the data over the network. This matches MITRE ATT&CK T1115 (Clipboard Data) — a technique used by Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) and other infostealers delivered via malicious agent skills. Legitimate skills do not need to exfiltrate clipboard content to remote servers.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1115/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1115/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"Skill reads clipboard contents and pipes or sends the data over the network. This matches MITRE ATT&CK T1115 (Clipboard Data) — a technique used by Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) and other infostealers delivered via malicious agent skills. Legitimate skills do not need to exfiltrate clipboard content to remote servers."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hardcoded base64 blob decoded and executed. Pattern shows a base64-encoded payload being decoded and piped to shell. This is obfuscated code execution."},"help":{"markdown":"Hardcoded base64 blob decoded and executed. Pattern shows a base64-encoded payload being decoded and piped to shell. This is obfuscated code execution.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Hardcoded base64 blob decoded and executed. Pattern shows a base64-encoded payload being decoded and piped to shell. This is obfuscated code execution."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Eval with base64 decode detected. Using eval on decoded base64 data is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious commands from static analysis."},"help":{"markdown":"Eval with base64 decode detected. Using eval on decoded base64 data is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious commands from static analysis.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Eval with base64 decode detected. Using eval on decoded base64 data is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious commands from static analysis."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill removes the macOS quarantine attribute from a downloaded file using `xattr -d com.apple.quarantine`. This bypasses Gatekeeper, which prevents execution of unsigned or unnotarized binaries from the internet. This technique was documented by 1Password and Trend Micro in the ClawHavoc campaign, where it was used to run the Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) without triggering macOS security warnings."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill removes the macOS quarantine attribute from a downloaded file using `xattr -d com.apple.quarantine`. This bypasses Gatekeeper, which prevents execution of unsigned or unnotarized binaries from the internet. This technique was documented by 1Password and Trend Micro in the ClawHavoc campaign, where it was used to run the Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) without triggering macOS security warnings.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass)\n - [https://1password.com/blog/from-magic-to-malware-how-openclaws-agent-skills-become-an-attack-surface](https://1password.com/blog/from-magic-to-malware-how-openclaws-agent-skills-become-an-attack-surface)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/b/openclaw-skills-used-to-distribute-atomic-macos-stealer.html](https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/b/openclaw-skills-used-to-distribute-atomic-macos-stealer.html)\n","text":"Skill removes the macOS quarantine attribute from a downloaded file using `xattr -d com.apple.quarantine`. This bypasses Gatekeeper, which prevents execution of unsigned or unnotarized binaries from the internet. This technique was documented by 1Password and Trend Micro in the ClawHavoc campaign, where it was used to run the Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) without triggering macOS security warnings."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill uses glot.io for malware distribution (ClickFix attack). This skill directs users to execute scripts from glot.io, a common malware distribution technique."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill uses glot.io for malware distribution (ClickFix attack). This skill directs users to execute scripts from glot.io, a common malware distribution technique.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting](https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting)\n","text":"Skill uses glot.io for malware distribution (ClickFix attack). This skill directs users to execute scripts from glot.io, a common malware distribution technique."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects execution of bash/sh with -c flag and pipe operations"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects execution of bash/sh with -c flag and pipe operations\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec](https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec](https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec)\n - [https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/](https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/)\n","text":"Detects execution of bash/sh with -c flag and pipe operations"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe.skill-go-exec-bash-pipe"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects bash reverse shell patterns using /dev/tcp"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects bash reverse shell patterns using /dev/tcp\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec](https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec](https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec)\n - [https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/](https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/)\n","text":"Detects bash reverse shell patterns using /dev/tcp"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec](https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec](https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec)\n - [https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/](https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/)\n","text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected fetch/axios followed by eval with data flow. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"help":{"markdown":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected fetch/axios followed by eval with data flow. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected fetch/axios followed by eval with data flow. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected download followed by exec/eval/subprocess on response data. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"help":{"markdown":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected download followed by exec/eval/subprocess on response data. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected download followed by exec/eval/subprocess on response data. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill instructs downloading password-protected executable (social engineering). This detects social engineering instructions to download and extract password-protected executables, a common malware distribution tactic."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill instructs downloading password-protected executable (social engineering). This detects social engineering instructions to download and extract password-protected executables, a common malware distribution tactic.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting](https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting)\n","text":"Skill instructs downloading password-protected executable (social engineering). This detects social engineering instructions to download and extract password-protected executables, a common malware distribution tactic."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Fetching executable content from a paste or code sharing service detected.\nThreat actors stage malicious scripts on free paste services to separate\nthe distribution channel from the payload, evading detection and allowing\npayload updates without modifying the delivery mechanism.\n\nPaste services (pastebin.com, hastebin, rentry.co, raw GitHub) are commonly\nused for secondary-stage payload hosting in supply chain attacks and the\nClawHavoc campaign. Using curl/wget to fetch raw content from these services\nfor execution is a high-confidence malicious indicator.\n\nIMPACT: Arbitrary code execution from attacker-controlled staging server\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Fetching executable content from a paste or code sharing service detected.\nThreat actors stage malicious scripts on free paste services to separate\nthe distribution channel from the payload, evading detection and allowing\npayload updates without modifying the delivery mechanism.\n\nPaste services (pastebin.com, hastebin, rentry.co, raw GitHub) are commonly\nused for secondary-stage payload hosting in supply chain attacks and the\nClawHavoc campaign. Using curl/wget to fetch raw content from these services\nfor execution is a high-confidence malicious indicator.\n\nIMPACT: Arbitrary code execution from attacker-controlled staging server\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1608/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1608/001/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting](https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting)\n","text":"Fetching executable content from a paste or code sharing service detected.\nThreat actors stage malicious scripts on free paste services to separate\nthe distribution channel from the payload, evading detection and allowing\npayload updates without modifying the delivery mechanism.\n\nPaste services (pastebin.com, hastebin, rentry.co, raw GitHub) are commonly\nused for secondary-stage payload hosting in supply chain attacks and the\nClawHavoc campaign. Using curl/wget to fetch raw content from these services\nfor execution is a high-confidence malicious indicator.\n\nIMPACT: Arbitrary code execution from attacker-controlled staging server\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Python exec on base64-decoded data. Using exec() on decoded base64 is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious Python code."},"help":{"markdown":"Python exec on base64-decoded data. Using exec() on decoded base64 is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious Python code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Python exec on base64-decoded data. Using exec() on decoded base64 is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious Python code."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately."},"help":{"markdown":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n","text":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess