-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n","text":"Detects bash reverse shell patterns using /dev/tcp"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n","text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"AWS credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates AWS access keys from the agent's runtime environment\nto an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation references (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<value>, table entries, etc.) are\nnot flagged; only actual variable reads combined with a network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full AWS credential exposure enabling account takeover\n"},"help":{"markdown":"AWS credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates AWS access keys from the agent's runtime environment\nto an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation references (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<value>, table entries, etc.) are\nnot flagged; only actual variable reads combined with a network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full AWS credential exposure enabling account takeover\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"AWS credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates AWS access keys from the agent's runtime environment\nto an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation references (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<value>, table entries, etc.) are\nnot flagged; only actual variable reads combined with a network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full AWS credential exposure enabling account takeover\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Azure credentials file access detected. Reading Azure credential files or tokens is a cloud credential theft technique."},"help":{"markdown":"Azure credentials file access detected. Reading Azure credential files or tokens is a cloud credential theft technique.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Azure credentials file access detected. Reading Azure credential files or tokens is a cloud credential theft technique."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Azure credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates Azure service principal credentials from the agent's\nruntime environment to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation setup examples (AZURE_CLIENT_ID=<app-client-id>) and legitimate\nAzure CLI usage (az login) are not flagged; only reads combined with a\nnon-Azure network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full Azure service principal credential exposure enabling subscription takeover\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Azure credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates Azure service principal credentials from the agent's\nruntime environment to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation setup examples (AZURE_CLIENT_ID=<app-client-id>) and legitimate\nAzure CLI usage (az login) are not flagged; only reads combined with a\nnon-Azure network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full Azure service principal credential exposure enabling subscription takeover\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Azure credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates Azure service principal credentials from the agent's\nruntime environment to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation setup examples (AZURE_CLIENT_ID=<app-client-id>) and legitimate\nAzure CLI usage (az login) are not flagged; only reads combined with a\nnon-Azure network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full Azure service principal credential exposure enabling subscription takeover\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Bitcoin wallet access detected. Reading Bitcoin Core wallet files (wallet.dat) or configuration is cryptocurrency theft."},"help":{"markdown":"Bitcoin wallet access detected. Reading Bitcoin Core wallet files (wallet.dat) or configuration is cryptocurrency theft.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Bitcoin wallet access detected. Reading Bitcoin Core wallet files (wallet.dat) or configuration is cryptocurrency theft."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Browser credential database access detected. Accessing Chrome, Firefox,\nSafari, or Edge password/cookie stores is a standard infostealer technique.\n\nChrome stores passwords in \"Login Data\" (SQLite) with encryption keys in\n\"Local State\". Firefox uses \"logins.json\" + \"key4.db\". These files contain\nall saved passwords and are targeted by commodity infostealers (Redline,\nVidar, AMOS) and by threat actor tools (Lazagne, HackerBrowserData).\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential compromise across all browser-saved accounts\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Browser credential database access detected. Accessing Chrome, Firefox,\nSafari, or Edge password/cookie stores is a standard infostealer technique.\n\nChrome stores passwords in \"Login Data\" (SQLite) with encryption keys in\n\"Local State\". Firefox uses \"logins.json\" + \"key4.db\". These files contain\nall saved passwords and are targeted by commodity infostealers (Redline,\nVidar, AMOS) and by threat actor tools (Lazagne, HackerBrowserData).\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential compromise across all browser-saved accounts\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/003/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/003/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Browser credential database access detected. Accessing Chrome, Firefox,\nSafari, or Edge password/cookie stores is a standard infostealer technique.\n\nChrome stores passwords in \"Login Data\" (SQLite) with encryption keys in\n\"Local State\". Firefox uses \"logins.json\" + \"key4.db\". These files contain\nall saved passwords and are targeted by commodity infostealers (Redline,\nVidar, AMOS) and by threat actor tools (Lazagne, HackerBrowserData).\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential compromise across all browser-saved accounts\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Cloud instance metadata service (IMDS) access detected. Accessing the\nmetadata service at 169.254.169.254 (AWS/Azure), metadata.google.internal\n(GCP), or equivalent endpoints returns temporary cloud credentials (IAM\nroles, service account tokens) that can be used to access cloud resources.\n\nIMDSv1 requires no authentication. The Capital One breach and many supply\nchain attacks exploited this. UNC2903 and other threat actors abuse IMDS\nto steal cloud credentials from compromised instances.\n\nIMPACT: Cloud credential theft, lateral movement to cloud infrastructure\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Cloud instance metadata service (IMDS) access detected. Accessing the\nmetadata service at 169.254.169.254 (AWS/Azure), metadata.google.internal\n(GCP), or equivalent endpoints returns temporary cloud credentials (IAM\nroles, service account tokens) that can be used to access cloud resources.\n\nIMDSv1 requires no authentication. The Capital One breach and many supply\nchain attacks exploited this. UNC2903 and other threat actors abuse IMDS\nto steal cloud credentials from compromised instances.\n\nIMPACT: Cloud credential theft, lateral movement to cloud infrastructure\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/005/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/005/)\n - [https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/cloud-metadata-abuse-unc2903/](https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/cloud-metadata-abuse-unc2903/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29](https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29)\n - [https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/cloud-security-atlas/attacks/stealing-ec2-instance-role-credentials/](https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/cloud-security-atlas/attacks/stealing-ec2-instance-role-credentials/)\n","text":"Cloud instance metadata service (IMDS) access detected. Accessing the\nmetadata service at 169.254.169.254 (AWS/Azure), metadata.google.internal\n(GCP), or equivalent endpoints returns temporary cloud credentials (IAM\nroles, service account tokens) that can be used to access cloud resources.\n\nIMDSv1 requires no authentication. The Capital One breach and many supply\nchain attacks exploited this. UNC2903 and other threat actors abuse IMDS\nto steal cloud credentials from compromised instances.\n\nIMPACT: Cloud credential theft, lateral movement to cloud infrastructure\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-918: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A10:2021 - Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Ethereum wallet access detected. Reading Ethereum keystore files is cryptocurrency theft. Keystore files are in ~/.ethereum/keystore/."},"help":{"markdown":"Ethereum wallet access detected. Reading Ethereum keystore files is cryptocurrency theft. Keystore files are in ~/.ethereum/keystore/.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-ethereum-wallet-read.skill-ethereum-wallet-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Ethereum wallet access detected. Reading Ethereum keystore files is cryptocurrency theft. Keystore files are in ~/.ethereum/keystore/."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-ethereum-wallet-read.skill-ethereum-wallet-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-ethereum-wallet-read.skill-ethereum-wallet-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-ethereum-wallet-read.skill-ethereum-wallet-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-ethereum-wallet-read.skill-ethereum-wallet-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"GCP credentials file access detected. Reading Google Cloud Platform credential files is a cloud credential theft technique."},"help":{"markdown":"GCP credentials file access detected. Reading Google Cloud Platform credential files is a cloud credential theft technique.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"GCP credentials file access detected. Reading Google Cloud Platform credential files is a cloud credential theft technique."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Solana wallet keypair access pattern found. Reading ~/.config/solana/id.json warrants investigation — it may indicate credential theft, but also appears in legitimate Solana agent integrations that require authorized wallet access. Verify whether this access is explicitly user-authorized."},"help":{"markdown":"Solana wallet keypair access pattern found. Reading ~/.config/solana/id.json warrants investigation — it may indicate credential theft, but also appears in legitimate Solana agent integrations that require authorized wallet access. Verify whether this access is explicitly user-authorized.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-solana-wallet-read.skill-solana-wallet-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Solana wallet keypair access pattern found. Reading ~/.config/solana/id.json warrants investigation — it may indicate credential theft, but also appears in legitimate Solana agent integrations that require authorized wallet access. Verify whether this access is explicitly user-authorized."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-solana-wallet-read.skill-solana-wallet-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-solana-wallet-read.skill-solana-wallet-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-solana-wallet-read.skill-solana-wallet-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-solana-wallet-read.skill-solana-wallet-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Full environment variable dump piped to network tool detected. The `env`\nor `printenv` command dumps ALL environment variables and piping them\ndirectly to curl/wget/nc sends the complete runtime context including all\nAPI keys, tokens, cloud credentials, and database URIs to an external host.\n\nThis differs from targeted grep-based harvesting: a full env dump captures\nevery secret in the process environment, including ones the attacker may\nnot have known to look for.\n\nIMPACT: Mass exfiltration of all runtime secrets and configuration\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Full environment variable dump piped to network tool detected. The `env`\nor `printenv` command dumps ALL environment variables and piping them\ndirectly to curl/wget/nc sends the complete runtime context including all\nAPI keys, tokens, cloud credentials, and database URIs to an external host.\n\nThis differs from targeted grep-based harvesting: a full env dump captures\nevery secret in the process environment, including ones the attacker may\nnot have known to look for.\n\nIMPACT: Mass exfiltration of all runtime secrets and configuration\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n - [https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/potential-data-exfiltration-through-curl.html](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/potential-data-exfiltration-through-curl.html)\n","text":"Full environment variable dump piped to network tool detected. The `env`\nor `printenv` command dumps ALL environment variables and piping them\ndirectly to curl/wget/nc sends the complete runtime context including all\nAPI keys, tokens, cloud credentials, and database URIs to an external host.\n\nThis differs from targeted grep-based harvesting: a full env dump captures\nevery secret in the process environment, including ones the attacker may\nnot have known to look for.\n\nIMPACT: Mass exfiltration of all runtime secrets and configuration\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network","id":"skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network","name":"skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hardcoded Discord webhook token or Telegram bot token detected. Threat actors\nembed real attacker-controlled credentials in malicious AI agent skills to\nsilently exfiltrate credentials, environment variables, and sensitive files.\n\nLegitimate notification skills that reference these APIs dynamically (via\nenvironment variables or user-supplied tokens) are NOT flagged by this rule.\nOnly hardcoded credential tokens in the standard formats are matched:\n  Telegram: bot{7-12 digits}:{30-50 alphanumeric chars}\n  Discord:  webhooks/{17-20 digit snowflake}/{60-80 char token}\n\nThese services blend in with HTTPS traffic and bypass network monitoring.\nThe ClawHavoc campaign and multiple npm malware families confirmed this vector.\n\nIMPACT: Silent credential and data exfiltration to attacker-controlled channels\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Hardcoded Discord webhook token or Telegram bot token detected. Threat actors\nembed real attacker-controlled credentials in malicious AI agent skills to\nsilently exfiltrate credentials, environment variables, and sensitive files.\n\nLegitimate notification skills that reference these APIs dynamically (via\nenvironment variables or user-supplied tokens) are NOT flagged by this rule.\nOnly hardcoded credential tokens in the standard formats are matched:\n  Telegram: bot{7-12 digits}:{30-50 alphanumeric chars}\n  Discord:  webhooks/{17-20 digit snowflake}/{60-80 char token}\n\nThese services blend in with HTTPS traffic and bypass network monitoring.\nThe ClawHavoc campaign and multiple npm malware families confirmed this vector.\n\nIMPACT: Silent credential and data exfiltration to attacker-controlled channels\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/)\n - [https://gbhackers.com/threat-actors-exploit-discord-webhooks-for-c2/](https://gbhackers.com/threat-actors-exploit-discord-webhooks-for-c2/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n - [https://thehackernews.com/2025/10/npm-pypi-and-rubygems-packages-found.html](https://thehackernews.com/2025/10/npm-pypi-and-rubygems-packages-found.html)\n","text":"Hardcoded Discord webhook token or Telegram bot token detected. Threat actors\nembed real attacker-controlled credentials in malicious AI agent skills to\nsilently exfiltrate credentials, environment variables, and sensitive files.\n\nLegitimate notification skills that reference these APIs dynamically (via\nenvironment variables or user-supplied tokens) are NOT flagged by this rule.\nOnly hardcoded credential tokens in the standard formats are matched:\n  Telegram: bot{7-12 digits}:{30-50 alphanumeric chars}\n  Discord:  webhooks/{17-20 digit snowflake}/{60-80 char token}\n\nThese services blend in with HTTPS traffic and bypass network monitoring.\nThe ClawHavoc campaign and multiple npm malware families confirmed this vector.\n\nIMPACT: Silent credential and data exfiltration to attacker-controlled channels\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2","id":"skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2","name":"skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for dangerous system commands.\nCommands like rm:*, dd:*, chmod:* with wildcards can cause system\ndamage, data loss, or privilege escalation.\n\nDETECTED: Dangerous command with wildcard\nIMPACT: Critical - System damage or privilege escalation\nRISK: Data destruction, permission manipulation, service disruption\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Avoid wildcards on destructive commands\n- Specify exact operations if truly needed\n- Consider safer alternatives\n- Document security justification\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for dangerous system commands.\nCommands like rm:*, dd:*, chmod:* with wildcards can cause system\ndamage, data loss, or privilege escalation.\n\nDETECTED: Dangerous command with wildcard\nIMPACT: Critical - System damage or privilege escalation\nRISK: Data destruction, permission manipulation, service disruption\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Avoid wildcards on destructive commands\n- Specify exact operations if truly needed\n- Consider safer alternatives\n- Document security justification\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.permission-escalation.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html)\n","text":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for dangerous system commands.\nCommands like rm:*, dd:*, chmod:* with wildcards can cause system\ndamage, data loss, or privilege escalation.\n\nDETECTED: Dangerous command with wildcard\nIMPACT: Critical - System damage or privilege escalation\nRISK: Data destruction, permission manipulation, service disruption\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Avoid wildcards on destructive commands\n- Specify exact operations if truly needed\n- Consider safer alternatives\n- Document security justification\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.permission-escalation.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard","id":"skills.permission-escalation.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard","name":"skills.permission-escalation.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-732: Incorrect Permission Assignment for Critical Resource","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.permission-escalation.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard.skill-dangerous-command-wildcard"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for network tools. Patterns like\nBash(curl:*) or Bash(wget:*) enable arbitrary network communication\nincluding data exfiltration.\n\nDETECTED: Network tool with wildcard (curl:*, wget:*, nc:*, etc.)\nIMPACT: High - Unrestricted network communication\nRISK: Data exfiltration to attacker-controlled servers\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Specify exact curl/wget operations needed\n- Example: Bash(curl:--request:GET) Bash(curl:--silent)\n- Avoid wildcards on network tools\n- Consider if network access truly required\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for network tools. Patterns like\nBash(curl:*) or Bash(wget:*) enable arbitrary network communication\nincluding data exfiltration.\n\nDETECTED: Network tool with wildcard (curl:*, wget:*, nc:*, etc.)\nIMPACT: High - Unrestricted network communication\nRISK: Data exfiltration to attacker-controlled servers\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Specify exact curl/wget operations needed\n- Example: Bash(curl:--request:GET) Bash(curl:--silent)\n- Avoid wildcards on network tools\n- Consider if network access truly required\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.permission-escalation.skill-network-bash-wildcard.skill-network-bash-wildcard)\n - [https://agentskills.io/specification#allowed-tools-field](https://agentskills.io/specification#allowed-tools-field)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html)\n","text":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for network tools. Patterns like\nBash(curl:*) or Bash(wget:*) enable arbitrary network communication\nincluding data exfiltration.\n\nDETECTED: Network tool with wildcard (curl:*, wget:*, nc:*, etc.)\nIMPACT: High - Unrestricted network communication\nRISK: Data exfiltration to attacker-controlled servers\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Specify exact curl/wget operations needed\n- Example: Bash(curl:--request:GET) Bash(curl:--silent)\n- Avoid wildcards on network tools\n- Consider if network access truly required\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.permission-escalation.skill-network-bash-wildcard.skill-network-bash-wildcard","id":"skills.permission-escalation.skill-network-bash-wildcard.skill-network-bash-wildcard","name":"skills.permission-escalation.skill-network-bash-wildcard.skill-network-bash-wildcard","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-732: Incorrect Permission Assignment for Critical Resource","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.permission-escalation.skill-network-bash-wildcard.skill-network-bash-wildcard"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill requests access to system persistence mechanisms via wildcards.\nCommands like crontab:*, systemctl:*, service:* enable installation\nof persistent backdoors that survive reboots.\n\nDETECTED: Persistence mechanism with wildcard\nIMPACT: Critical - Persistent backdoor installation\nRISK: Long-term system compromise, C2 communication\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Avoid wildcards on persistence mechanisms\n- Specify exact operations if legitimately needed\n- Document security justification clearly\n- Consider if persistence truly required for skill\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Skill requests access to system persistence mechanisms via wildcards.\nCommands like crontab:*, systemctl:*, service:* enable installation\nof persistent backdoors that survive reboots.\n\nDETECTED: Persistence mechanism with wildcard\nIMPACT: Critical - Persistent backdoor installation\nRISK: Long-term system compromise, C2 communication\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Avoid wildcards on persistence mechanisms\n- Specify exact operations if legitimately needed\n- Document security justification clearly\n- Consider if persistence truly required for skill\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.permission-escalation.skill-persistence-commands.skill-persistence-commands)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html)\n","text":"Skill requests access to system persistence mechanisms via wildcards.\nCommands like crontab:*, systemctl:*, service:* enable installation\nof persistent backdoors that survive reboots.\n\nDETECTED: Persistence mechanism with wildcard\nIMPACT: Critical - Persistent backdoor installation\nRISK: Long-term system compromise, C2 communication\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Avoid wildcards on persistence mechanisms\n- Specify exact operations if legitimately needed\n- Document security justification clearly\n- Consider if persistence truly required for skill\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.permission-escalation.skill-persistence-commands.skill-persistence-commands","id":"skills.permission-escalation.skill-persistence-commands.skill-persistence-commands","name":"skills.permission-escalation.skill-persistence-commands.skill-persistence-commands","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-732: Incorrect Permission Assignment for Critical Resource","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.permission-escalation.skill-persistence-commands.skill-persistence-commands"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for all tools. This pattern (*(*)\ngrants unrestricted access to all tool invocations.\n\nIMPACT: Critical - Unrestricted tool access\nRISK: Complete bypass of permission system\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Specify exact tools needed (Read, Write, Bash, etc.)\n- Use specific command patterns for Bash\n- Remove universal wildcards\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Skill requests wildcard permissions for all tools. This pattern (*(*)\ngrants unrestricted access to all tool invocations.\n\nIMPACT: Critical - Unrestricted tool access\nRISK: Complete bypass of permission system\n\nREMEDIATION:\n- Specify exact tools needed (Read, Write, Bash, etc.)\n- Use specific command patterns for Bash\n- Remove universal wildcards\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.permission-escalation.skill-wildcard-all-tools.skill-wildcard-all-tools)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definition